{"title":"2019 CIMC Problems/Part A Problem 2","text":"<div class=\"mw-content-ltr mw-parser-output\" lang=\"en\" dir=\"ltr\"><h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Problem\">Problem</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2019_CIMC_Problems/Part_A_Problem_2&amp;action=edit&amp;section=1\" title=\"Edit section: Problem\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>Binh has 20 quarters, worth 25 cents each. Abdul has 20 dimes, worth 10 cents each, as well as some quarters. If Binh and Abdul have the same amount of money, how many quarters does Abdul have?\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Solution_1\">Solution 1</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2019_CIMC_Problems/Part_A_Problem_2&amp;action=edit&amp;section=2\" title=\"Edit section: Solution 1\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>Since each quarter is worth <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/6/6/66644fd9f411299c3c1eabf151b5f601c9ef6c21.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$25$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"20\" height=\"14\" /> cents and Binh has <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/8/3/f8366cd6196dd8a9da6d38a3e9eafb109e99d53e.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$20$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"20\" height=\"14\" /> quarters, his coins are worth <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/d/8/d/d8d720686e5bdf09a78ec4d66395ca4b1c9217b1.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$25 \\times 20 = 500$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"112\" height=\"15\" /> cents in total.\n</p><p>Since each dime is worth <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/c/6/fc606f7f1e530731ab4f1cc364c01dc64a4455ee.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$10$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"20\" height=\"14\" /> cents and Abdul has <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/8/3/f8366cd6196dd8a9da6d38a3e9eafb109e99d53e.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$20$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"20\" height=\"14\" /> of them, his dimes are worth <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/b/9/5b950647b89e61f8535c938a8b9ce0705a209c90.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$10 \\times 20 = 200$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"112\" height=\"15\" /> cents in total. They have the same worth in total, so his quarters must be worth <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/3/7/437e504874f4859ae49590e77b59818578119f03.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$500 - 200 = 300$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"130\" height=\"15\" /> cents.\n</p><p>Thus, Abdul has <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/e/b/4eb0bf21e387f9eb28fe9def8569a48eb4391a8b.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\frac{300}{25} = \\boxed{12}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -13px\" width=\"87\" height=\"38\" /> quarters.\n</p><p>~anabel.disher\n</p>\n<table class=\"wikitable\" style=\"margin:0.5em auto; font-size:95%; border:1px solid black; width:80%;\">\n<tbody><tr>\n<td style=\"background:#ccf;text-align:center;\" colspan=\"3\"><b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2019_CIMC\" title=\"2019 CIMC\">2019 CIMC</a></b> (<b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2019_CIMC_Problems&amp;action=edit&amp;redlink=1\" class=\"new\" title=\"2019 CIMC Problems (page does not exist)\">Problems</a></b> • <b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2019_CIMC_Answer_Key&amp;action=edit&amp;redlink=1\" class=\"new\" title=\"2019 CIMC Answer Key (page does not exist)\">Answer Key</a></b> • <a rel=\"nofollow\" class=\"external text\" href=\"https://cemc.math.uwaterloo.ca/contests/past_contests.html\">Resources</a>)\n</td></tr>\n<tr>\n<td width=\"50%\" align=\"center\" rowspan=\"1\">Preceded&#160;by<br /><b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2019_CIMC_Problems/Part_A_Problem_1\" title=\"2019 CIMC Problems/Part A Problem 1\">Part A Problem 1</a></b>\n</td>\n<td width=\"50%\" align=\"center\" rowspan=\"1\">Followed&#160;by<br /><b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?